   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1940-05-18">May 18 th 40.</date></dateline>
               <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4051" type="person">Miss Marguerete Block</rs>.
               <lb/>401 Low Memorial Library <lb/>Colombia University <lb/><rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>. <salute>Dear <rs
                     ref="#tillich_person_id__4051" type="person">Miss Block</rs>,</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>My hesitation to write a review of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1783" type="person">Mr. Siegfried</rs>&apos;s
            book is not only caused by the lack of time (I have read it rather extensively). The real reason
            is that I do not know what to say about it. It is more big than impressive and I really do not
            know where to start and where to end. Do you not think it would be wise to drop it entirely?</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours</salute>
               
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
